  "critical_note": "With no coverage requirement (-c 0.0) MMseqs2 reports 100% identity for 4-9 residue LOCAL alignments against 12-26 residue peptides, flagging ~75% of EVERY portfolio including all three comparators. That is a short-alignment artifact of maximal sensitivity, not a real identity of 100%, and no sensible reading of 'no more than 80% sequence identity' means it. The grid below applies coverage requirements, which is what an organizer running MMseqs2 would do; MMseqs2's own default is -c 0.8.",
  "identity_definitions": {
    "pident": "MMseqs2 percentage identity over ALIGNED columns (its default reported identity)",
    "qcov_weighted": "pident * (alnlen/qlen) - identity discounted by how much of the peptide aligned, a stricter reading"
  },
